# Three images are built from this repo — apps/admin, apps/landing, apps/dashboard —
# and every one of them takes the repo root as its context (a pnpm workspace needs the
# lockfile and the workspace manifest above the app).
# Everything below is either rebuilt inside the image or has no business in it.

node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/dist
**/coverage
**/playwright-report
**/test-results

.git
.github
.conductor
.vercel
**/.vercel

# Secrets never enter the build context. The NEXT_PUBLIC_* values each app needs at
# build time are the one exception and arrive as apps/<app>/.env.production, allowed
# below — those values are inlined into a client bundle, so they are public by
# construction. A real credential does not go in one: the landing's DATABASE_URL, which
# its blog migrations need before the build, arrives as a BuildKit secret instead.
.env
.env.local
**/.env.local
**/.env*.local

!apps/admin/.env.production
!apps/landing/.env.production
!apps/dashboard/.env.production
